Xenia DXT/DXN interpolation: round to nearest instead of truncating.

The XDK documents the BC interpolants as integer expressions that round to
nearest:

  DXT1/DXT2-3/DXT4-5 colour  c2 = (2*c0 + c1 + 1) / 3
                              c3 = (c0 + 2*c1 + 1) / 3
  DXT5/DXN alpha, 8-step     a  = (k*a0 + (7-k)*a1 + 3) / 7
  DXT5/DXN alpha, 6-step     a  = (k*a0 + (5-k)*a1 + 2) / 5

XeniOS truncates instead (plain /3, /7 and /5), which puts the Metal BC
decompression one UNORM8 step below the Xenos reference on real Town fence
and M1911 textures. The refxenos CPU reference implements the documented
rounding, so the compute BC path is the one that is wrong.

Applied to the copied Xenia shader tree by
src/graphics/metal/tools/compile_metal_helpers.py; the upstream dep is not
modified.

